1. What is kubectl?
    - kubectl is the command-line tool used to interact with Kubernetes clusters.
    - Syntax:
        kubectl [command] [TYPE] [NAME] [flags]

2. Essential kubectl Commands:
    - Check cluster status: kubectl cluster-info
    - View nodes: kubectl get nodes
    - Create Pod: kubectl run nginx --image=nginx
    - List Pods: kubectl get pods -o wide
    - Watch live: kubectl get pods -w
    - Describe Pod: kubectl describe pod nginx
    - Delete Pod: kubectl delete pod nginx
    - Create Deployment: kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx
    - Scale Deployment: kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=3
    - Check Deployments: kubectl get deployments
    - Delete Deployment: kubectl delete deployment nginx
    - Apply YAML File: kubectl apply -f app.yaml
    - Delete Using YAML: kubectl delete -f app.yaml
    - View Logs: kubectl logs <pod-name>
    - Execute Inside Pod: kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- /bin/bash
    - List Namespaces: kubectl get namespaces
    - Create Namespace: kubectl create namespace dev
    - Use Namespace: kubectl get pods -n dev
    - View Current Context: kubectl config current-context
    - List Contexts: kubectl config get-contexts
    - Start cluster: minikube start
    - Deploy app: kubectl create deployment demo --image=nginx
    - Expose app: kubectl expose deployment demo --type=NodePort --port=80
    - View resources: kubectl get all
    - Open app: minikube service demo
